      "content": "Those symptoms—excessive thirst, frequent urination, and fruity or sweet-smelling breath—are classic signs of undiagnosed diabetes and could indicate a dangerous escalation of the condition. Because sugar in your urine can cause your breath to smell like spoiling fruit, this is unlikely to be simple dehydration and requires immediate medical attention. Please see a healthcare provider or go to an urgent care clinic as soon as possible to get blood sugar tested.",
